# Opsteady redirects.
#
# THIS FILE IS A PROBE. It exists to answer one question with evidence rather
# than documentation: does THIS deployment serve _redirects at all?
#
# Why the question is open. wrangler.toml declares only [assets] with a
# directory and not_found_handling; there is no redirect configuration. The repo
# has carried a `redirects.txt` for weeks, which nothing reads, and the redirects
# it documents have therefore never worked. Verified by direct fetch 2026-09-05:
#   https://opsteady.co.uk/catalogue          -> 404
#   https://opsteady.co.uk/interest.html      -> 404
#   https://opsteady.co.uk/site/pricing.html  -> 404
# That `_redirects` is the filename Cloudflare Workers Static Assets reads is an
# assertion from documentation, not evidence from this deployment.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO. It carries no rule that depends on the
# /interventions/ -> /modules/ rename. Every target below resolves in the
# structure that is live TODAY, so a visitor sees no change except that eight
# paths which currently 404 begin working. If _redirects turns out not to be read
# here, nothing has moved and nothing is lost.
#
# The rename's own rules follow in a second, separate publication, once this one
# has been proved.

# --- /catalogue: the first rename, whose redirects never fired --------------
/catalogue              /interventions/index.html                 301
/catalogue/:slug        /interventions/:slug.html                 301

# --- legacy interest page ---------------------------------------------------
/interest.html          /interventions/index.html                 301
/interest               /interventions/index.html                 301

# --- worked-example pages removed 2026-09-02 (see PROJECT_STATE.md) --------
# Repointed at the real page rather than a 301 chain into a 404.
/case-studies           /interventions/bottleneck_analysis.html   301
/case-studies/:slug     /interventions/bottleneck_analysis.html   301
/worked-examples/*      /interventions/bottleneck_analysis.html   301

# --- /site/*: dead since site/ was promoted to the repo root (86acb52) -----
# The Health Check's cross-links all point here and have been 404 ever since.
# /site/pricing.html -> /pricing.html, /site/interventions/index.html ->
# /interventions/index.html. Both exist today.
/site/*                 /:splat                                   301
